ut  having a buffer where you can start  tightening your purse strings and and  decide what to you know where to  prioritize your your finances  what people are telling us when they  come to food banks is that there aren't  any further cutbacks to make they're  sort of out of options and also food  bank managers are telling us that they  also feel that they're out of options  too that people are doing or they can  you know that they're trying to ensure  that they're claiming everything that  they're eligible for  they're budgeting  um they're prioritizing you know  what  they're on their household spending um  but there's nothing there's nothing  really left to do to manage the cost of  living crisis at the moment  and actually it we do we have seen that  in our network for a number of years now  for some people but what's really  concerning is that this is obviously  accelerating  gathering speed and we know that things  are set to get worse as has been said um  this autumn and so really now's the time  for the government to step in and show  that they recognize the sort of  emergency that's really unfolding now  for many people in our communities  all right we'll come back to you very  shortly adam says on the 5th of november  2020 the government canceled the job  retention bonus a 1 000 pound incentive  to employers to retain staff and  continue topping up their furlough what  happened to the retention incentive that  failed to materialize the many thousands  of pounds employers are owed have a  massively detrimental effect on  businesses is there any intention adam  asks to repay  the debt uh nina let's put that one to  you  i certainly don't think there is any  intention of bringing that back and i  think the the chancellor has been quite  definitive in the way he has talked  about that the justification being that  that was cancelled because the furlough  scheme was extended now you could it's  certainly valid to ask questions about  is it uh is it reasonable 